  "stem": "For \\(x \\neq 1\\) and \\(x \\neq -1\\), \\(\\frac{3}{x + 1} + \\frac{2}{x - 1} = \\frac{ax + b}{x^{2} - 1}\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(a + b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Use the common denominator \\((x + 1)(x - 1) = x^{2} - 1\\).",
    "The numerator is \\(3(x - 1) + 2(x + 1) = 3x - 3 + 2x + 2 = 5x - 1\\).",
    "So \\(a = 5\\) and \\(b = -1\\), and \\(a + b = 4\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nnum = Poly(expand(cancel((3/(x + 1) + 2/(x - 1))*(x**2 - 1))), x)\na, b = num.coeff_monomial(x), num.coeff_monomial(1)\nassert (a, b) == (5, -1)\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [a + b]",
